# Accessibility

Native HTML first. ARIA only when the host cannot express the role.
Behavior comes from `@ui8kit/aria` on kit primitives, not from a second widget tree.

## Structure

- A screen or chrome landmark **starts with `Block`**.
- Nested layout is never `Block`.
- Names come from `Label` or `aria-label`. Copy and `id` values are set in
  the app frame or passed as props.

## `@ui8kit/aria`

Register only the patterns this app uses in `src/lib/aria.ts`. Mark the host
primitive with the contract attributes. Do not invent a parallel JS API.

`package.json` → `ui8kit.aria` must stay `mode: "subset"` with
`dialog`, `disclosure`, `tooltip`, `alert`.

| Pattern | Primitive | Contract |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Dialog | `Dialog` | `data-ui8kit="dialog"`, open/close/overlay attrs, labelled |
| Disclosure | `Box` + `Button` | `data-ui8kit="disclosure"`, trigger + content |
| Tooltip | `Box` + `Text`/`Inline` | `data-ui8kit="tooltip"`, child `role="tooltip"` |
| Alert | `Alert` | `data-ui8kit="alert"` or `role="alert"` when urgent |

Do not put `data-ui8kit="disclosure"` on native `details` — that pattern
expects a trigger/content pair, not `<summary>`.

## Behavior

- One `main`. Skip to `id="main-content"`.
- Dialogs: name, description, focus, Escape, focus return.
- Routine status is polite. Failures may be `role="alert"`.
- Keep the kit focus ring.
- Theme is `light` / `dark` / `system` on `<html class="dark">`.

`bun run validate:ui8px-aria` must stay green.
